# MANIFOLD CARS 3D — COMPLETE PLAYER ACCESS CONTROL, ONBOARDING, LIVE PLAYER PRESENCE AND REAL-TIME IN-GAME CHAT IMPLEMENTATION

## PROJECT OVERVIEW

You are working on the existing MANIFOLD Cars 3D application.

Your assignment is to implement a complete registered-player gaming environment with controlled access, player onboarding, personalised vehicle configuration, real-time player discovery and private in-game communication.

This is a major feature implementation within the existing application.

You must work directly on the existing codebase.

Do not create a separate application.
Do not replace the existing Three.js game engine.
Do not create a disconnected mock interface.
Do not simulate player accounts or fake live users.

The existing application uses React, TypeScript, Three.js and Supabase. Inspect the actual project architecture and reuse its existing authentication, database, multiplayer and vehicle systems wherever possible.

## THE BUSINESS PURPOSE OF THE GAME

MANIFOLD is primarily an automotive discovery and visibility platform.

The 3D driving environment exists to give car dealers and their listed vehicles greater visibility, exposure and engagement through an immersive driving experience.

Players explore the Lagos-inspired driving environment, discover vehicles and experience the wider MANIFOLD automotive ecosystem.

The new social system should make the experience more interactive by allowing authenticated players to recognise and communicate with other real players driving nearby.

The game is not intended to become a dating platform or an unrestricted social network.

All communication must remain focused on ordinary, friendly in-game interaction.

