# PART 7 — TEN-MINUTE PLAYER INACTIVITY RULE

Only authenticated and genuinely active players may be discovered or contacted.

A player must become unavailable for chat if:

- They log out.
- Their authentication session expires.
- They disconnect.
- They remain inactive for ten minutes.

## 7.1 Heartbeat

Implement a heartbeat system.

Send a heartbeat every 30–60 seconds while the authenticated game session is active.

Update the last activity timestamp.

Use server-authoritative timestamps.

## 7.2 Inactivity handling

After ten minutes without a valid heartbeat or activity:

- Mark the player unavailable.
- Remove them from nearby player discovery.
- Stop displaying their active player identity.
- Prevent new chat invitations.
- Reject new messages.
- Expire outstanding invitations.
- Remove them from active chat availability.

A player who explicitly logs out must become unavailable immediately.

Do not rely exclusively on frontend timers.

Enforce availability through secure server-side checks.

## 7.3 Reconnection

When the player reconnects:

- Verify the session.
- Restore presence.
- Reload the player's current vehicle configuration.
- Resume discovery if eligible.

Do not automatically reopen expired invitations.

